CHAPTER V
RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE
Article 18
Women and children victims of violence shall receive the following rights: a. the right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected; b. the right to recovery;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality;
f. the right to social rehabilitation;
g. the right to complaint handling that is prompt, appropriate, comfortable and in accordance with their needs;
h. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process;
i. the right to assistance; and - 11 -
j. the right to security and protection.

Article 9
Regional Government conducts legal protection as referred to in Article 6 letter b, comprising:
a. providing protection in Safe Houses;
b. providing legal information to victims;
c. providing assistance for victims as witnesses from the investigation process until the verdict; and - 8 -
d. providing special legal protection for child victims of acts of violence which can be carried out through the appointment of guardianship in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
